          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಅಸಲಿ — asali — \"genuine; real\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಇದು ಅಸಲಿ ರೇಷ್ಮೆ ಅಂತ ಅಂಗಡಿಯವನು ಹೇಳಿದನು. idu asali rēṣme anta aṅgaḍiyavanu hēḷidanu. The shopkeeper said this is genuine silk."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Its opposite is ನಕಲಿ, a fake, from ನಕಲು, a copy."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಅಸಲಿ (asali) is usually traced to Arabic aṣl, \"root, origin\", through Hindustani aslī, \"original, genuine\"."
            }
          ]
        },
